# Data Fetching

### Do

Handle:

```text
Loading
Success
Empty
Error
```

Example:

```jsx
const InventoryPage = () => {
  const {
    items,
    loading,
    error,
    fetchInventory,
  } = useInventoryStore();

  useEffect(() => {
    let cancelled = false;

    const loadInventory = async () => {
      if (cancelled) {
        return;
      }

      await fetchInventory();
    };

    loadInventory();

    return () => {
      cancelled = true;
    };
  }, [fetchInventory]);

  if (loading) {
    return <InventorySkeleton />;
  }

  if (error) {
    return <ErrorState message={error} />;
  }

  if (!items.length) {
    return <EmptyState title="No inventory found" />;
  }

  return <InventoryTable items={items} />;
};
```

Follow the existing project's preferred data-fetching pattern when one exists.

### Don't

* Don't fetch the same data independently from multiple components.
* Don't ignore loading states.
* Don't ignore API errors.
* Don't update state after a component has been unmounted.

