# Stock Status

Use application-level status values.

Preferred values:

```text
in_stock
low_stock
out_of_stock
```

Map backend-specific values to these values.

Example:

```javascript
export const mapStockStatus = (status) => {
  switch (status) {
    case "IN_STOCK":
      return "in_stock";

    case "LOW_STOCK":
      return "low_stock";

    case "OUT_OF_STOCK":
      return "out_of_stock";

    default:
      return "unknown";
  }
};
```

### Don't

Don't compare backend enum values directly inside components.

Bad:

```jsx
{item.status === "OUT_OF_STOCK" && <Badge>Out of stock</Badge>}
```

Prefer:

```jsx
{item.stockStatus === "out_of_stock" && (
  <Badge>Out of stock</Badge>
)}
```

---

# Stock Movement

Preferred application-level movement types:

```text
purchase
sale
adjustment
transfer
return
damage
```

Use mapper functions when backend values differ.

Stock mutations should clearly communicate:

```text
Product
Warehouse
Current Quantity
Quantity Change
New Quantity
Reason
Movement Type
User
Date/Time
```

### Do

Support explicit operations such as:

```text
Receive Stock
Adjust Stock
Transfer Stock
Return Stock
Record Damage
```

Show confirmation for important or destructive operations.

### Don't

* Don't silently change stock quantities.
* Don't allow accidental double submissions.
* Don't modify inventory without showing appropriate feedback.
* Don't perform mutations without loading/error handling.

---

# Inventory Calculations

Keep calculations consistent.

Examples:

```text
Available Stock = Total Stock - Reserved Stock

Stock Value = Quantity × Cost Price

Low Stock = Quantity <= Reorder Level
```

Do not duplicate these calculations across multiple components.

If a calculation is used in multiple places, create a shared utility.

Example:

```javascript
export const calculateStockValue = (quantity, costPrice) => {
  return quantity * costPrice;
};
```

