# AI Coding Behaviour

Always:

* Think before generating code.
* Search the project before creating new files.
* Reuse existing components.
* Reuse existing hooks.
* Reuse existing services.
* Reuse existing stores.
* Reuse existing schemas and utilities.
* Match the existing code style.
* Keep diffs minimal.
* Preserve existing functionality.
* Check existing API services before creating new ones.
* Check existing components before creating duplicates.
* Verify API endpoint patterns before implementing new calls.
* Handle loading, error, and empty states.
* Handle permissions where applicable.
* Explain major architectural decisions when necessary.
* Prefer simple solutions over unnecessary abstractions.

Never:

* Invent APIs.
* Invent endpoints.
* Invent backend fields.
* Invent business rules.
* Duplicate components.
* Duplicate services.
* Rewrite unrelated code.
* Add unnecessary dependencies.
* Add unnecessary abstractions.
* Put API calls directly inside UI components.
* Hardcode API URLs.
* Hardcode secrets.
* Bypass authentication handling.
* Break existing functionality.
* Commit code unless explicitly requested.

